{"name":"Soap Pink","hex":"#e5bfca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic salt derived from a fatty acid, commonly used in cleaning products.","Some other substance, often a detergent or another surfactant, able to mix with both oil and water, used for cleaning."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply soap to in washing.","To cover, lather, or in any other manner treat with soap, often as a prank."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soap"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soap","blocks":[{"text":"Soap is a salt of a fatty acid used for cleaning and lubricating products as well as other applications. In a domestic setting, soaps, specifically \"toilet soaps\", are surfactants typically used for washing, bathing, and other types of housekeeping. In industrial settings, soaps are used as thickeners, components of some lubricants, emulsifiers, and catalysts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Handmade_soap_cropped_and_simplified.jpg/330px-Handmade_soap_cropped_and_simplified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soap"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm